  "answer": "Project Zenith has received a $2M budget approval from the executive board, though a later update indicates an adjustment to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses. The project team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, ahead-of-schedule testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics. The project is moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming activities including user interface enhancements in October, a staff meeting on November 20th to discuss the analytics report, and the implementation of updated security protocols (MFA and encryption) starting next January. Additionally, the team is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology integration."
